  "body": "Tormach's three routers. They are 3-axis machines run by PathPilot, so they likely post with the PathPilot mill dialect (confirm from the manual: spindle on/off words, units, tool changes, and any router-specific limits such as a manual tool change with no ATC).\n\nHub (PathPilot v2.14.4, 2026-11-09) lists this model under Current Machine Models. CamCraft does not ship it yet. Requested by the contributor so every Hub machine can be selected and Hub-tested.\n\n**Done means:** all three ship as Tormach machines with their manual figures, post through the PathPilot post (or a recorded router variant), and a Hub run of a simple profile passes on one of them.\n\nSpecs come from Tormach's operator manual for the model, its specifications table (contributor-supplied; cite the manual number and section in the decision file), clean-room. Same conventions as the shipped Tormach machines: inch, full-stroke-either-way travel, and a `tormach_machines`-style spec test.\n",
